# Keep the build context out of the image, and the host's state out of the build.
#
# The frontend stage does `COPY frontend/package*.json` + `npm ci` and only THEN
# `COPY frontend/ ./`, so without this file the host's frontend/node_modules
# overwrites the clean install and the bundle depends on whatever happens to be
# installed on the machine that runs `docker compose build`. That is not
# hypothetical: a build on 2026-09-12 produced two scanic-1.6 chunks from a tree
# whose lockfile pins scanic 1.0.6.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Built by the image itself; copying it in wastes context and can shadow the
# fresh build.
frontend/dist

# Runtime state. `data/` is a mounted volume — never bake a copy of the
# database, the documents or the rclone credentials into an image layer.
data
.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc

# Local-only
.env
.git
.gstack
.claude
test_documents
docs/screenshots
